<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THE DESCRIPTION BELOW IS CAPPED AT 255 CHARACTERS AND ONLY A DEPLOY CATCHES A BREACH -
        Jest, the SLDS linter and code review have all passed a 258-character one in this repo.
        It was counted before this file was written; count it again before editing it.

        Place on the Disposition record page only. recordId must be a Disposition__c Id, not a
        BOV_Submission__c or Broker_Assignment__c Id - see the component header.

        🔴 THAT SENTENCE IS NOW ENFORCED, NOT MERELY REQUESTED (code review W5, 2026-08-20). It used
        to be an instruction sitting in a comment while an actual targetConfig objects restriction
        existed one directory over, in dispositionBuyerTimeline. A misplaced instance would not have
        errored: the read is WHERE Disposition__c = :id, which matches no rows rather than throwing,
        so the card would have rendered its "No broker selected yet" empty state forever - and
        that empty state is the NORMAL case for most sales, so nobody would ever have suspected it.
    -->
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <!--
        masterLabel TRACKS THE CARD'S VISIBLE TITLE (`TITLE_BASE` in the JS) so an admin picking the
        component in App Builder sees the words that will appear on the page. Renamed 2026-08-25:
        "BOV Broker Change History" -> "Broker Selection", user-instructed. The "BOV" prefix was
        dropped as part of that match; App Builder lists ~22 other Broker* components, so the
        description below is what distinguishes this one - keep it specific.
        ⚠ "Broker Selection" is also a Disposition_Stage__c value and an approval process label.
        This card is NOT scoped to that stage; it lists every appointment and replacement ever
        recorded, including after the sale has left it.
        ⚠ THE DESCRIPTION WAS REWRITTEN 2026-08-25 (229 chars, re-counted) when the card gained its
        CURRENT SELECTION section: the old text promised replacements only, which is the same
        half-truth that made the card render "(0)" on a sale with an appointed broker.
    -->
    <masterLabel>Broker Selection</masterLabel>
    <description>The broker or brokers currently selected on this disposition, then every replacement recorded against it, newest first with reason and notes. A sale with no selection and no replacements shows a plain empty message, not an error.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__RecordPage</target>
    </targets>
    <targetConfigs>
        <targetConfig targets="lightning__RecordPage">
            <!-- The ELEMENT form; the objects= ATTRIBUTE form is rejected by the Metadata API. -->
            <objects>
                <object>Disposition__c</object>
            </objects>
        </targetConfig>
    </targetConfigs>
</LightningComponentBundle>
